        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{7}{2},\\ 1.5,\\ 11$",
          "worked": "$\\frac{7}{2}$ is a fraction of integers, $1.5=\\frac{3}{2}$ and $11=\\frac{11}{1}$, so these three numbers are rational. $\\sqrt{3}$ is irrational.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
